Multi-Agent Data Analysis System
Overview
This is a Streamlit-based web application that implements a multi-agent data analysis workflow using Groq's API. The system employs four specialized AI agents to perform comprehensive data analysis:

Data Preparation Agent: Cleans and preprocesses raw data
EDA Agent: Performs exploratory data analysis
Critic Agent: Reviews analysis outputs and provides feedback
Executor Agent: Validates results and provides final recommendations

Features

Interactive web interface built with Streamlit
Support for multiple data input methods:
Sample data
CSV file upload
Custom JSON data input


Data visualization using Plotly (line charts, bar charts, and pie charts)
Customizable model selection (LLaMA3-8b, LLaMA3-70b, Mixtral-8x7b)
Downloadable analysis results in JSON format
Persistent session state for viewing previous analysis results
Responsive design with custom CSS styling

Requirements

Python 3.8+
Streamlit
Requests
Pandas
Plotly
Groq API key (obtain from https://console.groq.com/)

Installation

Clone this repository:

git clone <repository-url>
cd <repository-directory>


Install dependencies:

pip install -r requirements.txt


Create a requirements.txt file with:

streamlit==1.25.0
requests==2.31.0
pandas==2.0.3
plotly==5.15.0

Usage

Run the application:

streamlit run app.py


Open your web browser and navigate to http://localhost:8501

In the sidebar:

Enter your Groq API key
Select a Groq model
Choose a data source (sample data, CSV upload, or custom JSON)


Click "Start Analysis" to run the multi-agent workflow


Configuration

The application uses a wide layout with an expanded sidebar
Custom CSS styles for enhanced visual presentation
API endpoint: https://api.groq.com/openai/v1/chat/completions
Default model parameters:
max_tokens: 1000
temperature: 0.7



File Structure

app.py: Main application file containing the Streamlit app and agent logic
Sample data generation for demonstration purposes
Visualization functions for data exploration

Output

Interactive visualizations of input data
Step-by-step analysis results from each agent
Downloadable JSON file containing all analysis results
Persistent view of previous analysis results

Notes

Ensure you have a valid Groq API key before running the application
The application requires an internet connection for API calls
Large datasets may increase processing time
Results are stored in session state and can be reviewed in the "Previous Analysis Results" section

